---
title: Configure & Regenerate Feature Flags
---

Now that you know how `VERA/Config/app-config.json` is structured, it's time to edit it in your local clone and regenerate the Swift source that the app actually reads.

## Edit a Flag

In your local clone of `vonage-video-ios-app`, open `VERA/Config/app-config.json` and change one or more flags in `meetingRoomSettings`. For example, turn off archiving, captions, and chat:

```json
{
  "meetingRoomSettings": {
    "allowArchiving": false,
    "allowCaptions": false,
    "allowChat": false
  }
}
```

Save the file once you've made your edit.

## Regenerate `AppConfig.swift`

From the `VERA/` directory of your local clone, run the builder:

```sh
./Scripts/builder.sh --update
```

The builder reads `Config/app-config.json`, writes the generated Swift source to `VERAConfiguration/VERAConfiguration/AppConfig.swift`, and regenerates the Xcode workspace.

| Script | Run from | Reads | Writes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `builder.sh --update` | `VERA/` | `Config/app-config.json` | `VERAConfiguration/VERAConfiguration/AppConfig.swift` and the Xcode workspace |

If the generated workspace is stale, run:

```sh
./Scripts/builder.sh --clean-and-update
```

{% aside type="caution" %}
If `app-config.json` has invalid JSON or is missing a required key, the builder stops with `Failed to generate AppConfig.swift.`

Fix `VERA/Config/app-config.json` and re-run `./Scripts/builder.sh --update` from `VERA/`.
{% /aside %}

Next, you'll rebuild the app in Xcode and confirm your changes.
